==Lines==

Currently, there are 12 subway lines and one [[automated guideway transit]] (AGT) line known as the "New Tram." The system spans {{cvt|503.3|km|mi|sp=us}} of subway track and {{cvt|8.7|km|mi|sp=us}} of AGT track, for a total of {{cvt|512.0|km|mi|sp=us}}, and serves 413 stations. Each line is identified by a letter code and a line color, which are used consistently across station signage, train livery, and passenger information displays.

A key feature of the Okami Metro is its extensive through-service agreements and physical track connectors with [[Okaiken Railways]] (OR) and private suburban operators. The [[Tozai Line (Okami)|Tozai Line]] connects with the [[Fukukyu Fukushima Line]] via the Toukai–Fukukyu Connecting Link and interfaces with regional commuter corridors across the east–west axis. The [[Asahi Line]] links directly with the [[Akitetsu Akita Line]] via the [[Akitetsu Asahi Line Connector]] near Enokigawa and Hiyori-cho, while the [[Chūō Line (Okami)|Chūō Line]] connects with the [[Okaden Toyohama Line]] at [[Koi Station|Koi]] via the Okaden Chuo Line Connector, and the [[Imaichi Line]] links to the [[Toukai Main Line]] corridor via the Toukai–Imaichi Rail Link at Kawabata Mon. In addition, the narrow-gauge ({{RailGauge|1067mm}}) [[Tokuyama Line]] operates reciprocal through-services with [[Okaiken Railways]] via the OR Tokuyama Line North Connector (at Mitani to the [[OR Iwashi Line]]) and the OR Tokuyama Line Metro Connector (at Hikari-cho to the [[OR Main Line]]), while the [[Nanboku Line (Okami)|Nanboku Line]] is scheduled to absorb and through-run with the [[Gomyo Railway Gomyo Line]] via its southern extension to Iwamura.

The network is structured around several major interchange hubs, including [[Okami Chuo Station|Okami Chūō]], where the Miyoshi, Chūō, and Shitayanagi lines converge; [[Hozumi-Oiwake Station|Hozumi-Oiwake]], where the Miyoshi, Tozai, and Asahi lines meet; and [[Rokumanji Station|Rokumanji]], where the Miyoshi, Tozai, and Nagata lines intersect. These hubs are among the busiest stations in the network, with several handling over 200,000 daily entries each.

