==Rolling stock==

Okami Metro operates a diverse fleet of rolling stock tailored to the specific technical requirements of its lines. Following the 2018 privatization, the company introduced a standardized classification system for its rolling stock, similar to the classification systems used by metro systems in China. This system categorizes trains into four types (A through D) based on car length, width, and capacity, plus a separate category for the AGT fleet. This standardization has streamlined procurement and maintenance, allowing for greater interoperability between lines that share the same type.

The majority of the network utilizes standard third-rail electrification (750 V DC). However, the [[Nagata Line]] and [[Imaichi Line]] utilize overhead catenary systems (1,500 V DC) to accommodate linear motor propulsion, which allows for smaller tunnel diameters and tighter curve radii in the dense older districts of the city. The [[Nankō Port Town Line]] uses 600 V AC three-phase third rail for its rubber-tired AGT vehicles.

