===Fleet overview===

The rolling stock fleet has evolved through several generations since the system's opening in 1935. The original [[Okami Metro 0 series|0 series]] trains, introduced for the opening of the Miyoshi Line in 1935, were retired in the 1960s and replaced by the [[Okami Metro 1000 series|1000 series]], which served as the second-generation fleet from 1961 through the 1990s before being fully retired. The third-generation [[Okami Metro 2000 series|2000 series]], introduced in 1981, was the mainstay of the Miyoshi and Tozai Lines for over three decades; it was refurbished in 2018 and is currently being phased out in favor of newer stock.

The [[Okami Metro 3000 series|3000 series]], introduced in 1990, was the system's first linear motor train, designed specifically for the Nagata and Imaichi lines. These trains are currently being retired and replaced by 5000 series stock. The [[Okami Metro 100 series|100 series]], introduced in 1981 for the Nankō Port Town Line AGT, was refurbished in 2018 and continues to serve as the sole AGT fleet.

The current mainstay of the fleet is the [[Okami Metro 5000 series|5000 series]], introduced in 2018 following the privatization. Manufactured by [[Okami Heavy Industries]], these trains serve as Type A and Type B stock for the Nanboku, Tokushige, Tokuyama, Asahi, Hitotsubashi, Miyoshi, and Nagata lines. The [[Okami Metro 6000 series|6000 series]], introduced in 2020, serves as Type C stock for the Tedorigawa, Shitayanagi, and Tozai lines. The [[Okami Metro 7000 series|7000 series]], the newest addition introduced in 2025, serves as Type D stock for the Chūō and Imaichi lines.

The flagship of the fleet is the [[Okami Metro 4000 series|4000 series]], introduced in June 2023 on the Miyoshi and Chūō lines. These trains feature a distinctive futuristic design reminiscent of a spacecraft, with hexagonal windows and onboard Wi-Fi integrated with the city's Satori Network. They were specifically commissioned to serve as the face of the transport network for the upcoming Expo. The 4000 series operates as a special variant of Type B and Type D stock, with enhanced passenger amenities and a unique exterior livery.

